Chapter
110 Christ Is Risen He will swallow up death in victory;
and the Lord God will wipe away tears
from off all faces; . . . And it shall be said in that day,
Lo, this is our God.
(Isa. 25:8-9.)
Trust ye in the Lord for ever:
for in the Lord Jehovah is everlasting strength. . . . Thy dead men shall live,
together with my dead body shall they arise. Awake and sing, ye that dwell in dust:
for thy dew is as the dew of herbs,
and the earth shall cast out the dead. . . . The earth also shall disclose her blood,
and shall no more cover her slain.
(Isa. 26:4, 19, 21.)
There is no saviour beside me. . . . I will ransom them from the power of the grave;
I will redeem them from death:
O death, I will be thy plagues;
O grave, I will be thy destruction.
(Hosea 13:4, 10, 14.) "Death Is Swallowed Up in Victory" And now the dawn!
